.Dd $Mdocdate: September 5 2026 $
.Dt MOUNT_BTRFS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount_btrfs
.Nd mount a Btrfs file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Op Fl s Ar subvolid
.Ar special node
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
command attaches the Btrfs file system on the device
.Ar special
to the file system namespace at
.Ar node .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl o Ar options
Specify a comma-separated list of mount options.
See
.Xr mount 8
for the available options.
.It Fl s Ar subvolid
Select an existing subvolume by its numeric tree ID.
The default, also selected by zero or 5, is the top-level tree.
The on-disk default subvolume setting is not used.
.El
.Pp
Multiple mounts of the same device may be writable simultaneously if
their selected subvolume hierarchies are disjoint.
A selected tree cannot equal, contain, or be contained by another
mounted tree.
In particular, a top-level mount excludes all other mounts of that device.
Nested subvolumes remain accessible through their containing mount,
and each subvolume's read-only flag is honored.
.Pp
Mounts of one device share allocation and a transaction.
Syncing or unmounting any view may commit changes made through other views.
The device remains open until the last view is unmounted.
A read-only view may join a filesystem opened writable.
If the first view was read-only, all views must be unmounted before
mounting a writable view.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mount 2 ,
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr umount 8
.Sh CAVEATS
The driver supports a limited subset of Btrfs formats and write operations.
Mount updates, subvolume creation, and subvolume property changes are
not supported.
